<http://data.silknow.org/event/e377140b-4410-3c8b-ab9b-7b15caa2603d>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This cream satin programme with gilt metallic fringe was produced for Queen Victoria's first State Visit to the theatre, printed in black ink with a royal crest. The programme began with Rossini's opera <i>Il Barbiere di Siviglia</i> starring Madame Grisi, Signor Mario, Signor Lablache and Signor F. Lablache, a <i>Pas de Deux</i> between the acts by Fanny Elssler and  Mlle. Cerito, and the ballet <i>Ondine ou La Naiade</i> danced by Mlle Cerito, Mlle Camille, Mlle Scheffer, Mlle Planquet, Mlle Benard, Mlle Galby, Mlle Ducie, Mlle CVopere, Mlle Guy Stephen, M. St. Leon and M. Perrot, with scenery by Mr. William Grieve. Her Majesty's Theatre, 20 July 1843."@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/1153b8a8-c681-393e-9e8c-fbfb72f8b6eb> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This cream satin programme with gilt metallic fringe was produced for Queen Victoria's first State Visit to the theatre, printed in black ink with a royal crest. The programme began with Rossini's opera <i>Il Barbiere di Siviglia</i> starring Madame Grisi, Signor Mario, Signor Lablache and Signor F. Lablache, a <i>Pas de Deux</i> between the acts by Fanny Elssler and  Mlle. Cerito, and the ballet <i>Ondine ou La Naiade</i> danced by Mlle Cerito, Mlle Camille, Mlle Scheffer, Mlle Planquet, Mlle Benard, Mlle Galby, Mlle Ducie, Mlle CVopere, Mlle Guy Stephen, M. St. Leon and M. Perrot, with scenery by Mr. William Grieve. Her Majesty's Theatre, 20 July 1843."@en .

